.TH PLEASE 1 "August 2026" "Please" "User Manuals"
.SH NAME
please \- An AI-native git CLI. You never type raw git commands.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B please
.RI "<command> [args...]"
.br
.B please
.RI """<what you want to do>"""
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B please
is an AI-native git CLI. Git remains the engine underneath;
.B please
is the interface. It uses an AI agent (Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, or OpenAI ChatGPT) to handle staging, commit messages, and pushing on your behalf.
.PP
Typos and filler words don't block a command either. A typo'd command word is recognized if it's one edit away from a real command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B please commit
Stages your changes, sends the diff to the AI, and lets it split the work into one or more logically coherent commits.
.TP
.B please push
Runs commit, then pushes the current branch to origin.
.TP
.B please status
A plain-language view of where you stand.
.TP
.B please branch [name]
List local branches or create and switch to a new branch.
.TP
.B please switch <name>
Switches to an existing branch or creates it.
.TP
.B please sync [exactly]
Fetches and merges the current branch's upstream. With 'exactly', discards local commits not on the remote.
.TP
.B please undo / redo
Undoes the last commit, or brings it back.
.TP
.B please move-commit <branch>
Moves your last commit onto a new branch.
.TP
.B please discard
Throws away all uncommitted changes, tracked and untracked.
.TP
.B please stash
Saves everything in the working tree, tracked and untracked, and clears it.
.TP
.B please squash [n | ref]
Combines a run of commits into one, AI-written message and all.
.TP
.B please purge <path>
Permanently removes a file or folder from your entire git history.
.TP
.B please chat
The agent kept alive across multiple messages for interactive sessions.
.TP
.B please man <command>
View detailed manual page for a specific command inside the terminal.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.please/config
Global configuration for AI provider and model choices.
.br
.I .git/PLEASE.MD
Local repository context for the AI.
